# OmniGrid — Workspace rules (pointer)

Full guidelines live in `AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md` at this repository's root — read it before editing.
Each package also carries its own `AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md`. This file keeps the essential invariants
close at hand for Cursor.

## Non-negotiable architecture

1. `omnigrid/core` is HEADLESS and framework-agnostic: no DOM globals, no React/Vue/Svelte,
   no DOM mutations, zero runtime dependencies. It must run in Node without a browser.
2. Adapters (e.g. `adapters/react`) are the ONLY layer that touches the DOM — and they
   must NOT re-implement core logic (sorting, filtering, grouping, pagination, virtualization).
3. Styling is CSS-variable + absolute-positioning based (`transform: translateY(...)` for row
   recycling); the core never emits styles or DOM.
4. Scroll position is ephemeral: scroll-only `setViewport({ scrollTop, scrollLeft })` must NOT
   notify the Store / re-render adapters. Structural changes bump `getRevision()`.

## Plugins

5. Plugin logic is framework-agnostic. Implement `GridPlugin<T>`: `name` + `register(api)` that
   returns a full cleanup function.
6. Mount UI through the Slot Architecture: `api.slots.mount(slot, content, options)` with headless
   `SlotContent` declarations — never manual DOM inside a plugin.
7. Hook the pipeline via `api.registerDataProcessor((data: T[]) => T[])`, subscribe via
   `api.on(...)`, read state via `api.getState()`.

## Pro & licensing

8. Pro plugins live in the private `omnigrid-pro/` repo (`@omnigrid/plugin-pro`);
   `plugins/pro/` in this repo is an empty stub. Base plugins are MIT in `plugins/base/*`.
9. Validate `licenseKey` LOCALLY: Ed25519 signature checked with an embedded public key via Web
   Crypto — no runtime network calls. Invalid/missing → throw and never enable the feature;
   the grid stays functional. Never put license logic in `omnigrid/core`.

## Workflow

10. Run `npm test` after changes and follow the existing Prettier/ESLint config and test patterns
    (vitest, headless for core/plugins). Use `@api` doc comments on public plugin APIs.
11. Update package READMEs / `AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md` files when public contracts change; search
    existing types before designing new APIs.